{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\n\nOperator decisions supersede this ticket's original framing (see comments). **2026-08-10:** do NOT\nretune the fuzzy `low|medium|high` boundary — ordinal labels are an LLM anti-pattern (models do not\napply them reliably for deterministic gate behavior); replace each ladder with a closed KIND set\nmapping deterministically to floor-vs-advisory. **2026-08-12:** do both halves now — drop the\ninert-G5 hedge (no bump) AND land the conversion under its own `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` bump. Per\n**C11** (`.../ordinal-migration-plan.md` Phase 1) the plan-v5 batch is both axes plus the margin\nrider.\n\nCorpus evidence (persisted REVIEW_RESULT sidecars): every non-none grade on both axes floors impact\nto 0.85 (`_PLAN_HARD_OVERRIDE_FLOOR` in `decide.py`), so `low` == `high`. Of `undecomposed`'s 30\ngraded bodies, 23 are \"this plan bundles N independently-releasable outcomes\" — a right-sizing note on\nan executable plan — yet each floors; 4 blocked. `dod_uncertifiable` is\ngraded 1,413 times, mixing three distinct defects under one blind floor. The hedge is inert:\n`veto_undecomposed_g5` fired ZERO times. `ORACLE_GRADE01` (v3) / `DIVERGENCE_GRADE01` (v4) are the\nprecedents.\n\n## What\n\n**Scope is ONE unit, not a bundle to split.** ADR 0054 section 4 requires impact-model shape changes\nbatched behind one `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` bump, since each bump closes the current cohort. Items 2-3\nare shape changes; 1 and 4 are no-bump riders otherwise stranded from their evidence. NOT\nindependently releasable.\n\n1. **Prompt rewrite (no bump).** Delete the inert G5-suppressor hedge from both prompts and the\n   `undecomposed` description in `verify_models.py`; both prompts' bullets for these axes are also\n   REWRITTEN (see Steps) to enumerate the six kinds and their pick rules.\n2. **`undecomposed` -> kind set (bump):** `none`; `bundles_separable_slices` — executable as written\n   but packs outcomes that could each ship alone, so splitting only aids clarity — contributing\n   `UNDECOMPOSED_BUNDLED_CONTRIB` = 0.55, NEVER flooring; `missing_required_child` — work the plan\n   or its parent commits to has NO child/sibling — flooring; `no_executable_breakdown` — no\n   executable step sequence for its scope, or an all-or-nothing build whose riskiest unknown is not\n   de-risked — flooring.\n3. **`dod_uncertifiable` -> kind set (bump):** `none`; `underspecified_certification` — the outcome\n   IS certifiable and an oracle exists, but its exact command/path/assertion is not stated —\n   contributing `DOD_UNDERSPECIFIED_CONTRIB` = 0.55, NEVER flooring; `uncertifiable_outcome` — a\n   committed outcome has NO acceptance criterion, test or proving mechanism — flooring;\n   `certification_cannot_prove` — a stated mechanism cannot establish the outcome (names something\n   nonexistent or unable to detect what is claimed, or a trivially broken implementation satisfies\n   it) — flooring.\n4. **Decision-margin telemetry (no bump).** Record `priority - block_threshold` per finding in the\n   sidecar. C11 P0.2 says `impact_sev`, but `pass3_decide` blocks on `priority >= block_threshold`\n   (`priority = validity x impact`), so the margin uses `priority`. Additive only.\n5. **Bump `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` plan-v4 -> plan-v5** in `plan_review/sidecar.py`.\n\n**Evidence gate before landing (zero LLM).** Add a re-score script under `docs/calibration/`\ncovering every recorded finding under the new maps and reporting old-vs-new flips. It reads persisted `severity_attributes` as RAW dicts (never through the new `Literal` model, which rejects\nthe old labels). **Mapping rule:** each recorded grade maps to a kind by ORDERED regex over the\nfinding's own prose + evidence (first match wins), GAP-BIASED — a body describing a missing, broken\nor vacuous oracle, or missing required decomposition maps to a FLOORING kind; only a\nspecificity/framing complaint maps to advisory. Rows matching no rule are scored BOTH ways, so the result is a BOUND, not a point estimate. Per the R1 bar, a lost block is\nUNJUSTIFIED iff the body describes such a gap yet re-maps to advisory; any such flip means ESCALATE,\nnot land.\n\n## Steps\n\nImplement items 1-5 in order, then 6-8.\n\n`_SEV01` maps only `none|low|medium|high`, returning 0.0 for any kind name. `impact_plan` reads\nthese axes through `_SEV01` in THREE places, and ALL THREE must be rewritten against the new\n`*_GRADE01` maps or the axes silently go dead: the contribs MAX (via `_PLAN_SEVERITY_AXES`), the\n`has_override` floor loop (via `_PLAN_HARD_OVERRIDE_AXES`), and the `dod_uncertifiable` amplifier\nforce of `mult = 1.0`. Adding both to `_PLAN_GRADED_AXES` covers the first two; the amplifier force\nis a separate rewrite.\n\nThe verifier EMITS these values, so both prompts' bullets for these axes are REWRITTEN to enumerate\nall six kinds with pick-this-kind rules and advisory-vs-flooring semantics, matching the existing\n`divergent_implementation` bullet's form.\n\n6. In `tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py` REWRITE (not merely extend) the pre-existing ordinal-keyed\n   cases for these axes — `test_hard_override_floors_low_axis_to_085`,\n   `test_each_ordinal_override_axis_triggers_floor`,\n   `test_dod_uncertifiable_forces_full_detection_weight` — to kind names, then add the new cases;\n   update `test_impact_model_versioning.py`; pin the margin in `test_plan_review_sidecar.py`.\n   `test_criteria_vocabulary_reviewers.py` pins \"success criterion\" in the `dod_uncertifiable`\n   bullet, so PRESERVE that phrasing.\n7. Update `docs/plan-review-gate.md` (lines 225-235): its \"present at any grade\" narrative describes\n   exactly the flooring behavior items 2-3 replace. Extend the paragraph already documenting the\n   plan-v3 oracle split to cover both kind sets.\n8. Write the re-score script; record rules + results in `docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md`.\n\nOut of scope: `veto_undecomposed_g5` removal, C11 Phase 2. Gates: `make lint && make typecheck`, the\nAC commands, `python -m pytest tests/interfaces -q -k plan_review`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Both axes are closed `Literal` kind sets. Verified: `python -m pytest\n      tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py -q -k literal` passes, asserting each annotation holds the six\n      kind names and none of `low`/`medium`/`high`.\n- [x] Each advisory kind contributes 0.55 and never floors; each gap kind yields 0.85; both CONTRIB\n      constants sit strictly below the lowest blocking `block_threshold` (0.6) in\n      `criteria_routing.json`, like `UNDERSPECIFIED_ORACLE_CONTRIB`; the amplifier\n      still forces `mult = 1.0` for non-none `dod_uncertifiable`. Verified: `python -m pytest\n      tests/unit/test_impact_plan.py -q` passes with cases pinning both advisory kinds at 0.55, the\n      four gap kinds at 0.85, the contrib-below-0.6 invariant, and `self_revealing` +\n      `underspecified_certification` at 0.55 not 0.44.\n- [x] No prompt or description cites the G5 suppressor, and `docs/plan-review-gate.md` no longer\n      says these axes floor at any grade. Verified: `rg -n \"deterministic G5 signal already|signal\n      already suppresses\" src/rebar/` and `rg -n \"is present at any\" docs/plan-review-gate.md` both\n      exit 1.\n- [x] The sidecar records a per-finding `priority - block_threshold` margin, and\n      `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` is `plan-v5` batched per ADR 0054 section 4. Verified: `python -m pytest\n      tests/unit/test_plan_review_sidecar.py tests/unit/test_impact_model_versioning.py -q` passes\n      (including a `-k margin` case), and the commit body names the hedge removal, both conversions\n      and the margin telemetry as riding one bump.\n- [x] The re-score is landed and shows no unjustified lost blocks (rule above). Verified:\n      `docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md` states the mapping rules and reports old-vs-new counts\n      under both residual bounds plus the audited loss list, and `python\n      docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py --root=<checkout>` reproduces them. (Path corrected:\n      `/reports/` is gitignored, so a script there could never land — see comment.)"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786518108963579001,"uuid":"16c73997-4b92-4b22-98a6-cdda41e2fa11"}